    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d925">

                <pb facs="0871" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/1124a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-05T21:00:00-04:00">June 5, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>510. British Embassy here has informed Department of telegraphic correspondence
                    between your British colleague and Foreign Office in connection with passage of
                    German ships through Straits and relation of protest on this development to
                    exchange of notes referred to in Department’s 494, June 1. Department assumes
                    that you will act in concert with your British colleague and take no independent
                    action with respect to exchange of notes until his existing instructions have
                        <pb facs="0872" n="860" xml:id="pg860"/> been confirmed or altered. In
                    latter case Department will promptly instruct you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
